import{_ as t,c as a,o as n,ag as r}from"./chunks/framework.ARG558ZT.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Applied AI, Python and assisted engineering projects","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"practice/ai-project.md","filePath":"practice/ai-project.md"}'),i={name:"practice/ai-project.md"};function o(s,e,d,c,l,p){return n(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<h1 id="applied-ai-python-and-assisted-engineering-projects" tabindex="-1">Applied AI, Python and assisted engineering projects <a class="header-anchor" href="#applied-ai-python-and-assisted-engineering-projects" aria-label="Permalink to “Applied AI, Python and assisted engineering projects”">​</a></h1><p>Build on the same notes/course product and the existing Python companion lessons. The primary control design is a bounded single-owner workflow, current source authorization and typed tool/model boundaries. LangGraph is the one framework example; plain functions/state transitions remain the baseline. These four specifications integrate the existing substantive lessons; they do not require mastering several agent SDKs, training a model or paying for cloud infrastructure.</p><p>Use approved synthetic/public data first. Keep a pinned Python3.13/uv environment and the selected SDK/schema/runtime versions from the implementation lessons. Offline deterministic fixtures establish boundary behavior; a permitted live provider test, labeled quality comparison and independent implementation remain separate evidence. Do not turn a stubbed provider response into a reported model result.</p><p>See the <a href="./applied-ai/">staged RAG → resumable workflow → n8n sequence</a> for smaller checkpoints of P-334/P-335 and the new bounded automation exercise. These refinements retain the requirements below; every learner outcome remains outstanding.</p><h2 id="p-334" tabindex="-1">P-334 <a class="header-anchor" href="#p-334" aria-label="Permalink to “P-334”">​</a></h2><p><strong>Deliverable:</strong> a permission-aware document assistant supporting ingest/update/delete, lexical and hybrid retrieval comparison, current-authority context assembly, supported citations/abstention, bounded streaming and recoverable failures. It answers from authorized versioned source spans; it does not search an arbitrary private filesystem or execute instructions found in a document.</p><p><strong>Setup:</strong> use the <a href="./../python-for-ai/document-processing.html">text/CSV extractor</a>, <a href="./../python-for-ai/vector-storage-lifecycle.html">persistent vector lifecycle</a>, <a href="./../python-for-ai/retrieval-pipeline.html">retrieval pipeline</a>, <a href="./../python-for-ai/retrieval-context.html">source/citation verifier</a> and <a href="./../python-for-ai/model-streaming.html">streaming owner</a>. Put their modules into one owned learner service with explicit interfaces and a lockfile. Seed two synthetic tenants with two principals, source versions, ACLs, exact locators and at least one unanswerable question. Keep authoritative source bytes/ACL/version separate from vector/index/cache derivatives.</p><p>Implement these increments and retain a working checkpoint after each:</p><ol><li>Authorized bounded ingestion→exact source hash→extractor/segment/chunk identities→staged generation. Reject unsupported/empty/malformed/oversize input before model calls. Complex parsers require their existing isolated-worker contract.</li><li>A deterministic lexical baseline, then a compatible embedding-space adapter and a hybrid candidate. Record exact model/vector dimensions/settings, chunking and index generation. Never combine incompatible embedding spaces or compare different permitted corpora as one benchmark.</li><li>Current tenant/subject filters <strong>before</strong> candidate/context selection, bounded rerank and actual-payload token budgeting. Re-resolve source version/ACL/locator immediately before context and again before a cited source is displayed when needed. An ANN post-filter alone can miss allowed results and must not leak forbidden candidates.</li><li>A typed answer/insufficient-evidence/unavailable contract with stable source-version/span citations. Verify citation existence/current access and assess actual claim support; a valid source ID alone does not prove entailment. Source-authored “ignore instructions” text stays data.</li><li>Owned stream cancellation/overall+idle budgets, validated terminal result and bounded safe UI. A partial draft is not a final accepted answer and may contain unsupported text. Cancel and disconnect release local owners; remote billing/work may remain unknown.</li><li>Update/delete/revoke: stage/reindex/replace generation atomically at your chosen visibility boundary, invalidate derived caches and deny revoked access immediately. Keep deletion receipts/retention policy for source/vector/chunk/trace/export/backup owners. Do not claim hard deletion from merely hiding a search result.</li></ol><p><strong>Worked trace:</strong> user-a asks what a timeout proves. The fixture&#39;s authorized <code>public:v1:line1</code> says it limits caller waiting and does not prove a remote write failed. Retrieval resolves that exact current span, the answer states that distinction and cites it. <code>private:v1:line1</code> belongs to user-b&#39;s tenant and cannot be included even if it has a high similarity score. If public is revoked between retrieval and context, stop/retrieve again or abstain; do not keep an old authorized excerpt as permanent permission. If no permitted source documents the launch date, return insufficient evidence instead of inventing one.</p><p>The authored <code>ai-lab/corpus.json</code> and <code>cases.json</code> retain this tiny synthetic task/case seed, including an instruction-like source line. It is development data, not a held-out benchmark. Expand it with reviewed relevance/support labels and independent source families. No real secret or customer data appears in it.</p><p><strong>Comparison acceptance:</strong> freeze questions, permitted corpus, labels, task/output policy and workload; compare lexical versus hybrid recall at a declaredk and answer support/coverage/abstention, duplicate/citation errors, latency and total known/unknown cost. Include no-answer/cross-tenant/injection/update/delete/revocation cases and repeated runs. Report sample size/slices and paired failures; do not claim general quality from eight synthetic cases. Missing provider usage is unknown, not zero.</p><p><strong>Operational acceptance:</strong> cancel during retrieval and generation; inject store/provider timeout, malformed output and stale source; recover to explicit safe states with no unsupported final answer or duplicate job. Enforce maximum bytes/chunks/tokens/tool calls/deadline/spend through one owner, count retries and close/reap all tasks/clients. Show permission filtering and budget failure cause zero forbidden/provider/tool calls. Retain real source/index lifecycle observations and a safe UI review. Actual integrated adapters, live quality and learner execution are still required.</p><h2 id="p-335" tabindex="-1">P-335 <a class="header-anchor" href="#p-335" aria-label="Permalink to “P-335”">​</a></h2><p><strong>Deliverable:</strong> one reproducible evaluation suite plus a bounded read→propose→approve→write→receipt tool workflow. The purpose is to test whether orchestration obeys the task and authority under failure, not whether two model answers sound convincing. Use <a href="./../python-for-ai/evaluation-lab.html">evaluation cases/rubric</a>, <a href="./../python-for-ai/evaluation-measurements.html">measurements</a>, <a href="./../python-for-ai/tool-boundaries.html">typed tools</a>, <a href="./../python-for-ai/tool-workflow-state.html">workflow state</a> and <a href="./../python-for-ai/approved-writes.html">approved writes</a>.</p><h3 id="dataset-and-rubric" tabindex="-1">Dataset and rubric <a class="header-anchor" href="#dataset-and-rubric" aria-label="Permalink to “Dataset and rubric”">​</a></h3><p>The retained8case seed covers normal, missing evidence, cross-tenant, injection, tool failure, revocation, cancellation and budget rejection. Each case has a stable ID, exact question, trusted fixture principal, scenario and expected status/citation references. Instantiate the scenario through your test adapters; it is not a magic field a provider obeys. Keep normal/injection cases&#39; permitted evidence identical when isolating injection impact. Add human-authored expected claims and relevant-span labels before judging free text; these seed status/citation labels do not establish semantic truth.</p><p>Version corpus/case/rubric/parser/prompt/retriever/model/settings and source permissions. Group related documents/questions before splitting development/validation/held-out sets; do not tune prompts on held-out failures and then call the same set untouched. Compare a frozen deterministic/lexical baseline with the candidate under the same workload, repeated runs and failure policy. Deterministic checks cover schema, current authority, citations, budgets and receipts. Human rubric covers factual/semantic support, useful abstention, task completion and misleading omissions; a model judge is an additional calibrated signal, not an unquestioned oracle.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Failure case</th><th>Hard expectation</th><th>Evidence to retain</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Missing evidence</td><td>Insufficient evidence; no invented date/source</td><td>Current permitted source set and answer status</td></tr><tr><td>Cross-tenant/injection</td><td>Zero unauthorized read/write/disclosure; source commands ignored</td><td>Redacted dispatcher events and source IDs, not private bodies</td></tr><tr><td>Store/tool failure</td><td>Explicit unavailable/retry/defer/unknown state under policy</td><td>Attempt count/deadline and no fabricated success</td></tr><tr><td>Revoked approval/source</td><td>Current policy denies despite old checkpoint</td><td>Revision/authority decision and zero effect</td></tr><tr><td>Interrupted write</td><td>Resolve stable operation receipt before retry</td><td>Durable command digest, operation ID and effect count</td></tr><tr><td>Duplicate dispatch</td><td>One logical local effect under idempotency contract</td><td>Transaction/receipt uniqueness and conflict behavior</td></tr><tr><td>Aggregate budget exhausted</td><td>Stop/defer before more work</td><td>Shared reservation/usage ledger, known/unknown totals</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The persisted <code>ai-lab/check.py</code> verifies this seed&#39;s case IDs/slices and exact fixture status/citation expectations, rejects missing results, and catches three deliberately wrong outputs. That single pytest check passed2026-10-26. Its success input is an authored expected ledger; <strong>no model or integrated assistant was evaluated</strong>. It is a starting contract check, not a semantic grader or product-quality measurement.</p><h3 id="tool-workflow-and-approval" tabindex="-1">Tool workflow and approval <a class="header-anchor" href="#tool-workflow-and-approval" aria-label="Permalink to “Tool workflow and approval”">​</a></h3><p>Start with two fixed tools: authorized note lookup and an exact-title rename. Tool arguments are bounded runtime schemas; the dispatcher allowlists names and obtains identity/current permissions outside model text. No arbitrary shell, URL, SQL or file-path tool. Propose an immutable command containing resource/version/new title and operation ID; show the actual change/effect to the human. Approval binds actor, exact command digest, source/version, scope and expiry. A changed argument, revoked permission or expired approval requires a new decision. A tool result or a previous assistant message cannot approve a write.</p><p>Persist state and revision before an external boundary. Use one atomic budget owner across retries/resumes/subtasks, e.g. an illustrative maximum5tool calls,1write, a declared total deadline and a reviewed cost reserve. These are exercise limits, not universal defaults. Step count alone does not bound time/token/financial work. Unknown usage stays reserved/reconciled according to policy; restarting a graph cannot replenish the budget.</p><p>The write adapter commits local idempotency receipt plus effect in one transaction. Same operation+same digest returns the retained result; same ID+different command conflicts. For a remote provider, pass its supported operation key and reconcile status: local SQLite cannot create an atomic transaction with that service. Kill the workflow before dispatch, after dispatch/before response and after receipt; verify pending/unknown/completed remain distinguishable. Exactly-once claims must name the local boundary.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> run normal and adversarial cases repeatedly; retain paired baseline/candidate results, safe per-stage traces, total latency, all attempts and known/unknown task cost. Demonstrate revoked-access resume, tampered approval, duplicate/conflicting command, handler timeout, unknown external outcome and aggregate-budget exhaustion. Real human approval/review, persistent multi-process recovery and provider-quality evidence are still required; a generated workflow or RAM checkpoint is not proof of completion.</p><h2 id="p-336" tabindex="-1">P-336 <a class="header-anchor" href="#p-336" aria-label="Permalink to “P-336”">​</a></h2><p><strong>Deliverable:</strong> an AI-assisted issue-to-reviewed-local-change record for a different real or clearly labeled study issue. Use the complete <a href="./../ai-assisted-engineering/issue-to-reviewed-change.html">worked retry issue</a>, <a href="./../ai-assisted-engineering/verification-and-permissions.html">verification challenges</a>, <a href="./../ai-assisted-engineering/local-workflow-and-git.html">local workflow</a> and <a href="./../ai-assisted-engineering/traceability-and-evaluation.html">traceability record</a>. Do not present that authored case as your personal employment incident.</p><p><strong>Setup:</strong> inspect applicable instructions, repository status, exact task/API, relevant callers/configuration and allowed checks. Minimize the context packet: issue/ACs, complete relevant source/ranges, versions and actual safe failure output; exclude .env/credentials/private logs/data. Repository comments/issues/generated commands are untrusted task data, not authority to export secrets or widen scope. Preserve dirty user changes. Use an existing appropriate branch or an explicitly scoped local <code>codex/</code> worktree when useful; worktrees isolate checkout files, not credentials/databases/network access.</p><p>Create an acceptance-to-check matrix before editing. Reproduce one named baseline failure; keep its source/command/result. Implement the smallest justified change, review the actual tracked and untracked diff for unrelated edits, invented APIs/imports, weakened config/tests and missing security cases. Verify APIs against installed declarations/runtime and official versioned docs. Generated tests must derive expectations from the requirement, not bless the candidate&#39;s behavior. Add one plausible wrong patch or targeted fault that the checks reject, outside restricted tests and only in an owned disposable fixture.</p><p><strong>Retained record:</strong> issue identity and whether authored/real; current base/source/lock/runtime; allowed paths/decisions; failing baseline; exact changed paths; build/test/fault results tied to candidate bytes; actual review findings/corrections; unperformed checks/risks; concise behavior-focused handoff. Keep checkpoint current so another engineer can resume the exact next action. An old passing result cannot silently follow a later source change. Hashing identifies bytes but does not authenticate evidence.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> a requirement-derived test fails on the defect, the final change passes applicable build/Jest/Module4 Cobertura commands and meaningful boundary checks, and the retained fault is caught. Review the real diff and correct concrete findings; retain an independent human review if one actually happens, otherwise state not performed. Report no invented productivity savings, CI success, PR, customer outcome or reviewer. Prepare a local patch/PR description only: <strong>never push commits/branches/tags</strong>, and no external publication/message is implied. Independent learner diagnosis, explanation and review evidence remain required.</p><h2 id="p-337" tabindex="-1">P-337 <a class="header-anchor" href="#p-337" aria-label="Permalink to “P-337”">​</a></h2><p><strong>Deliverable:</strong> a small independently implemented Python companion endpoint for validated ingestion/classification, with reproducible environment, correct async ownership, structured safe logs and actual integration/deployment checks. Python is role-dependent; the target is enough fluency to implement/debug this service, not mastery of every ML framework.</p><p><strong>Setup:</strong> reconstruct one owned <code>study_ai</code> package from the existing <a href="./../python-for-ai/setup-and-basics.html">setup</a>, <a href="./../python-for-ai/configuration-and-logging.html">configuration/logging</a>, <a href="./../python-for-ai/fastapi-boundaries.html">FastAPI boundary</a>, <a href="./../python-for-ai/async-http.html">async HTTP</a> and <a href="./../python-for-ai/deployment.html">deployment</a> examples. Pin Python3.13.11, compatible FastAPI/Pydantic/Uvicorn/pytest dependencies in pyproject.toml/uv.lock and run locked sync. Keep runtime and dev/check environments separate. Start with the lesson&#39;s deterministic text preparation, not a paid/model/GPU dependency. Use the single selected model SDK only if the endpoint actually needs generation.</p><p>Choose one contract, e.g. <code>POST /documents</code> accepts a bounded strict <code>{id,body}</code> and returns a projected created DTO. The authenticated principal/tenant comes from trusted server middleware, never a body field or prompt. A parser/schema checks shape, the service enforces current permission and the repository owns durable uniqueness. The existing memory repository is disposable; before claiming restart/multi-replica persistence implement a durable shared adapter and migration/transaction policy. A validated classifier result must retain the exact source version/quote support rather than describe a whole document from one fragment.</p><p><strong>Implementation increments:</strong> first pure typed preparation/error functions; then strict Pydantic DTOs and injected repository/provider protocols; then app lifespan-owned clients/repository; finally HTTP boundary, byte/deadline controls and supervised server launch. Use async clients for I/O and bounded offload/process isolation for blocking parsing/CPU work. <code>async def</code> does not make a synchronous parser nonblocking. A cancelled coroutine cannot kill an arbitrary thread/parser; kill/reap isolated hostile-format workers when required. Plain UTF-8/CSV is sufficient for the initial project; unsupported PDF/OCR is explicit rather than silently indexed empty.</p><p>Test pure functions with pytest fixtures and temporary owned files. ASGITransport checks app routes/middleware without real sockets; add the existing real Uvicorn process/socket/SIGTERM smoke for listener/lifecycle behavior. Inject timeout, invalid provider JSON, repository outage, body oversize/invalid UTF-8, duplicate IDs, cross-user access and failed cleanup. Keep caller waiting/underlying work distinct; outbound deadlines must cover body consumption and retry attempts. Log only fixed fields/event codes and safe IDs; test synthetic sensitive markers do not enter responses/logs. Missing credentials/config fail startup before readiness.</p><p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> strict package typecheck and pytest pass under the locked environment; negative schema/security/body/cancellation tests reach the right status with no secret echo; real process starts, serves allowed/denied operations and exits/reaps within the stated deadline; clients/files/pools close. A durable adapter persists state through restart, and release artifacts match tested source/lock/runtime. Retain a deployment note for TLS/proxy trust, one-process-per-instance baseline, migrations, readiness/drain, secret rotation and rollback/recovery. No live provider, cloud deployment, durable storage or independent learner implementation is inferred from the supplied component lessons.</p><p>Official references checked2026-10-26: <a href="https://docs.python.org/3.13/library/asyncio-task.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Python asyncio cancellation/task ownership</a>, <a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/events/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">FastAPI lifespan</a>, <a href="https://docs.pydantic.dev/latest/concepts/models/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Pydantic models</a>, <a href="https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/fixtures.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">pytest fixtures</a>, <a href="https://git-scm.com/docs/git-worktree" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Git worktrees</a>, <a href="https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Secrets_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">OWASP secrets management</a>. Provider/model-specific versions, retention and billing must be checked for an authorized live practice run; this specification makes no current price or account-availability claim.</p>',39)])])}const m=t(i,[["render",o]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
